#N canvas 100 100 700 600 10;
#X obj 40 40 jet_win;
#X msg 40 80 create;
#X msg 130 80 destroy;
#X obj 40 130 jet_head 0;
#X obj 40 165 jet_color 1 0.5 0.2;
#X obj 40 200 jet_circle 2;
#X floatatom 40 250 5 0 5 0 - - -;
#X text 40 275 radius;
#X msg 140 250 size 1;
#X msg 220 250 size 3.5;
#X obj 340 130 jet_head 1;
#X obj 340 165 jet_perlin 128 128;
#X obj 340 200 jet_translateXYZ -3.6 -2.4 0;
#X obj 340 235 jet_circle 1.4;
#X text 480 165 <- a texture fills the circle;
#X text 40 330 [jet_circle] is a filled circle like Gem's [circle]\, but its edge is smooth at any size - the pixel shader cuts the disc out of a quad and fades the last pixel\, so there are no polygon corners. radius is in Gem units (the window is 8 units tall). It is centred on the origin of the chain\, so move it with jet_translateXYZ\; scale x and y differently with jet_scaleXYZ and you get an ellipse (or use [jet_ellipse]).;
#X text 40 460 Inlets\: the chain (bang \, plus "size r") and the radius (it only stores - drawing happens on the next bang). Colour from jet_color (alpha makes it translucent)\, a current texture is shown inside the circle. The bang is forwarded.;
#X connect 1 0 0 0;
#X connect 2 0 0 0;
#X connect 3 0 4 0;
#X connect 4 0 5 0;
#X connect 6 0 5 1;
#X connect 8 0 5 0;
#X connect 9 0 5 0;
#X connect 10 0 11 0;
#X connect 11 0 12 0;
#X connect 12 0 13 0;
